Input: {"question": "Which award did Eugene I. Shakhnovich receive?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 33, "text": "**Renowned Biophysicist Eugene I."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 34, "end": 108, "text": "Shakhnovich Honored with Prestigious Canada Gairdner International Award**"}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 110, "end": 249, "text": "Toronto, Canada - In a ceremony held at the historic Fairmont Royal York hotel, the Canada Gairdner Foundation announced yesterday that Dr."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 250, "end": 259, "text": "Eugene I."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 260, "end": 389, "text": "Shakhnovich, a distinguished Soviet and American biophysicist, has been awarded the esteemed Canada Gairdner International Award."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 390, "end": 514, "text": "This prestigious recognition is bestowed upon scientists who have made outstanding contributions to medical science, and Dr."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 515, "end": 631, "text": "Shakhnovich's groundbreaking work in the field of protein folding and misfolding has earned him this esteemed honor."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 632, "end": 635, "text": "Dr."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 636, "end": 843, "text": "Shakhnovich, currently a professor of chemistry and chemical biology at Harvard University, has dedicated his career to understanding the intricacies of protein structures and their role in various diseases."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 844, "end": 1063, "text": "His pioneering research has shed light on the molecular mechanisms underlying protein misfolding, which is implicated in a range of debilitating conditions, including Alzheimer's, Parkinson's, and Huntington's diseases."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1064, "end": 1214, "text": "\"I am deeply humbled to receive this award, and I am grateful to the Canada Gairdner Foundation for recognizing the significance of our research,\" Dr."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1215, "end": 1258, "text": "Shakhnovich said in an exclusive interview."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1259, "end": 1470, "text": "\"This honor is not just a recognition of my own work, but also a testament to the tireless efforts of my colleagues and collaborators who have contributed to our understanding of protein folding and misfolding.\""}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1471, "end": 1686, "text": "The Canada Gairdner International Award is considered one of the most prestigious awards in the field of medical science, with past recipients including Nobel laureates and leading researchers from around the world."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1687, "end": 1690, "text": "Dr."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1691, "end": 1839, "text": "Shakhnovich's award is accompanied by a $100,000 prize, which he plans to use to further his research and support the next generation of scientists."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1840, "end": 1844, "text": "\"Dr."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1845, "end": 1993, "text": "Shakhnovich's work has opened up new avenues for understanding and potentially treating some of the most devastating diseases of our time,\" said Dr."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1994, "end": 2077, "text": "Janet Rossant, President and Scientific Director of the Canada Gairdner Foundation."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2078, "end": 2224, "text": "\"His contributions to the field of biophysics have been truly transformative, and we are delighted to recognize his achievements with this award.\""}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2225, "end": 2386, "text": "According to data from the National Institutes of Health, protein misfolding is implicated in over 50 different diseases, affecting millions of people worldwide."}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2387, "end": 2390, "text": "Dr."}, "D1S23": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2391, "end": 2573, "text": "Shakhnovich's research has focused on developing novel computational models and experimental approaches to understand the complex processes underlying protein folding and misfolding."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 87, "text": "Here is a Wikipedia-style entry that presents comprehensive evidence for the statement:"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 89, "end": 98, "text": "Eugene I."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 99, "end": 110, "text": "Shakhnovich"}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 112, "end": 121, "text": "Eugene I."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 122, "end": 238, "text": "Shakhnovich is a Soviet and American biophysicist who has made significant contributions to the field of biophysics."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 239, "end": 263, "text": "Early Life and Education"}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 265, "end": 384, "text": "Shakhnovich was born in the Soviet Union and received his undergraduate degree in physics from Moscow State University."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 385, "end": 410, "text": "He later earned his Ph.D."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 411, "end": 451, "text": "in biophysics from the same institution."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 452, "end": 458, "text": "Career"}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 460, "end": 566, "text": "Shakhnovich's research focuses on the application of physical principles to understand biological systems."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 567, "end": 707, "text": "He has held faculty positions at several prestigious institutions, including Harvard University and the University of California, San Diego."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 708, "end": 725, "text": "Awards and Honors"}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 727, "end": 815, "text": "Shakhnovich has received numerous awards and honors for his contributions to biophysics."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 816, "end": 896, "text": "One of his notable awards is the Packard Fellowship for Science and Engineering."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 897, "end": 943, "text": "Packard Fellowship for Science and Engineering"}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 945, "end": 1130, "text": "The Packard Fellowship for Science and Engineering is a prestigious award that recognizes early-career scientists and engineers who have demonstrated exceptional promise in their field."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1131, "end": 1281, "text": "The fellowship is awarded annually by the David and Lucile Packard Foundation to support innovative research in the fields of science and engineering."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1282, "end": 1299, "text": "Evidence of Award"}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1301, "end": 1374, "text": "According to the David and Lucile Packard Foundation's website, Eugene I."}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1375, "end": 1458, "text": "Shakhnovich was awarded the Packard Fellowship for Science and Engineering in 1996."}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1459, "end": 1599, "text": "[1] This award is a testament to Shakhnovich's outstanding contributions to the field of biophysics and his potential for future innovation."}, "D2S23": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1600, "end": 1611, "text": "References:"}, "D2S24": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1613, "end": 1653, "text": "[1] David and Lucile Packard Foundation."}, "D2S25": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1654, "end": 1661, "text": "(n.d.)."}, "D2S26": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1662, "end": 1678, "text": "Packard Fellows."}}, "original_cards": [], "current_answers": ["Canada Gairdner International Award", "Packard Fellowship for Science and Engineering"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Canada Gairdner International Award", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Packard Fellowship for Science and Engineering", "origin": "initial"}]}

